  "term": "ECT",
  "definition": "ECT, or electroconvulsive therapy, is a treatment procedure that passes brief electrical currents through the brain through electrodes to produce a controlled seizure. It is used for severe mental illness that has been difficult to treat, including depression, mania, and catatonia.",
